      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This study was designed to examine whether theophylline, an adenosine receptor antagonist, affects cardiac adaptation to ischemia during progression of repetitive balloon inflations of percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA). Theophylline abolished this cardiac adaptation, suggesting that endogenous adenosine is a key mediator for cardiac adaptation during PTCA."},
